# 🚀 Automated Web Hosting Using Shell Script

A simple Linux automation project that automatically installs and configures the Apache2 web server, downloads a website template, extracts the website files, and deploys the website to the Apache web root using a Bash shell script.

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to automate website hosting on a Linux server using a Shell Script. Instead of manually installing a web server and configuring website files, the script performs the deployment process with a single execution.

The project uses the **Orbital website template from Tooplate** as the sample website.

## ✨ Features

- ⚙️ **Automated Installation** — Installs Apache2, Unzip, and Curl.
- 🌐 **Web Server Configuration** — Starts and enables Apache2 at boot.
- 📥 **Automatic Download** — Downloads the website template ZIP file.
- 📦 **File Extraction** — Extracts the website template to the web directory.
- 🚀 **Automatic Deployment** — Places the website files in `/var/www/html`.
- 🔄 **Service Restart** — Restarts Apache2 after deployment.
- 🐧 **Linux Administration** — Demonstrates practical Linux command-line skills.

